claimed: acme-dns-providers -- finishing the DNS story (operator: 'доделай'). Three `Acme.Dns` implementations, not one: Cloudflare (Bearer token, /client/v4/zones/<zone>/dns_records), deSEC (Token header, PUT rrsets with an empty records list as the delete) and Route 53 (the repo's OWN SigV4 from okay-blob with service=route53, ChangeResourceRecordSets UPSERT/DELETE) -- three, because the reason none shipped was that ONE favourite baked into a seam is worse than none, and three with a credential each is a menu rather than a favourite. Every credential is a `Secret`, every failure is the provider's own sentence, every propagation default is that provider's documented one and overridable. Tested by SHAPE against a stub server that asserts what we send and answers what the provider would (no account can be had in a test), on top of the dns-01 flow already proven with challtestsrv. Touches okay-acme (a new Providers.scala), build.sbt (okayBlob for the signer), specs/acme.md, docs.
